name:Ecce sacerdos magnus;
office-part:Graduale;
mode:5;
book:Graduale O.P. (Paredes), 1928: Supplementum S.R.C. 1933 bound in the 1928 copy, leaf p. 1 (djvu 314 right), S. Alberti Magni (15 Nov.) (same chant in Graduale O.P. 1950, p. 616);
transcriber:read note by note from the scan of the 1933 supplement leaf for this site, second pass done;
commentary:Text and punctuation as printed on the leaf. The custos at the end of staff 3 stands at e, but staff 4 begins with the clivis hg; the notes are followed;
